    safetyLevel: "warning",
    summary: "CMV consensus 2025: dose by kidney-function bands; in CMV treatment, leukopenia alone: antiviral dose cut not recommended; options include adjusting other myelosuppressive drugs (call the transplant team first).",
    body: "\u2022 **Below normal kidney function use the [kidney dose bands](#/info/tpe-cmv-dosing)** (Cockcroft-Gault, mL/min): frequent kidney-function monitoring is recommended (strong, moderate); reduce the antiviral dose only for worsening kidney function (strong, low). [17]\n\u2022 **During CMV treatment, leukopenia alone:** reducing the antiviral dose is not recommended (strong, moderate); options include G-CSF and adjusting other myelosuppressive drugs (call the transplant team first). Labels say avoid below stated counts: [Guideline and label differ](#/info/tpe-cmv-dosing). [17, 19, 20]\n\u2022 Changing antivirals is not recommended in the first 2 weeks if clinically improving, even with unchanged or rising DNA (strong, moderate); DNA commonly rises in week 1. [17]\n\u2022 Transfusion: leukoreduced or CMV-seronegative blood products are recommended, especially in D\u2212/R\u2212 recipients (strong, moderate). [17]\n\u2022 Oral ganciclovir, acyclovir and valacyclovir are not recommended for treatment (strong, moderate). [17]\n\u2022 Letermovir: dose reduction is required with cyclosporine; may alter tacrolimus levels; close monitoring is needed. [17]",
